## 4. The four builds as compact "preset cards" (so the hero swap isn't repeated four times)

Beneath/around the bus rails, four small **patch-preset chips**, each a miniature of the same bay showing only the *delta*:

- **A — BLOWN-SLEEP DEADLINE (Modafinil):** eject caffeine · keep theanine solo · keep choline+structural · skip huperzine. Badge: **CYCLICAL — swing weapon · repay the sleep.**
- **B — LEARNING SPRINT (Noopept *or* Aniracetam):** ease/halve huperzine · lean on choline · keep modest caffeine+theanine · *Aniracetam adds:* take with fatty breakfast. "Pick one, not both." Badge: **CYCLICAL.**
- **C — DAILY RITUAL (Semax ± gated nicotine):** **eject nothing** (Semax has no ejector spring — additive) · optional nicotine behind the context-gate. Badge: **DAILY-CAPABLE.**
- A small **"fat-solubility"** glyph on Aniracetam (an oil-drop bound to the breakfast) — its one distinct mechanic.

**Daily vs cyclical coding (load-bearing, not decorative):** additive / non-tolerance levers (Semax, gated nicotine) carry a **steady-glow DAILY badge**; the swing weapons (modafinil, noopept, aniracetam) carry a **momentary / spring-return CYCLE badge** that visibly resets — the literal expression of *"anything that resets your baseline floor upward is a swing weapon by definition."*

**The nicotine gate (amber, set apart):** nicotine sits behind a small **`WORK CUE ONLY` gated door** with a slow **tolerance-creep meter** and a **managed-dependence** amber tag — "the gating is the clever part; it stops the cue generalising." Drawn as an honest trade, never endorsed or villainised.

